From 74e442231c0b2f1ad9a7dd3aa08a7bce4c2e4674 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <winshyon@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 17:28:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: allow soft pod anti-affinity for dev and test clusters

cass-operator schedules at most one Cassandra pod per Kubernetes node, so
a 3-replica Instance never becomes Ready on a single-node k3d/kind
cluster (#23). Add an optional softPodAntiAffinity boolean to the engine
component's parameters and map it onto the K8ssandraCluster's
softPodAntiAffinity (cass-operator's allowMultipleNodesPerWorker).

- The field is set at the cluster level next to Resources and merged
  into the datacenter by k8ssandra-operator; its webhook rejects a
  datacenter-level softPodAntiAffinity without datacenter-level resources.
- cass-operator requires CPU and memory requests and limits when the
  option is on, while the UI only sets limits and the default resources
  leave CPU unlimited, so a missing request is filled from its limit and
  vice versa; a resource with neither is rejected in Validate.
- cass-operator forbids changing allowMultipleNodesPerWorker on a live
  datacenter, so toggling it after creation fails Sync with a clear
  error instead of every later apply being rejected by the webhook. The
  UI toggle is disabled in edit/restore mode.
- Left unset, the field is omitted entirely, so default behavior and
  existing clusters are unchanged.

The toggle is exposed in the Advanced UI section with a production
warning, and the provider spec is regenerated with `make generate`.
